# 📚 Lesson 38 Everything except the weather

## 💡 【New words and expressions】(6)

| 单词 | 词性 | 含义 |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **except** | prep. | 除了 |
| **Mediterranean** | n. | 地中海 |
| **complain** | v. | 抱怨 |
| **continually** | adv. | 不断地 |
| **bitterly** | adv. | 刺骨地 |
| **sunshine** | n. | 阳光 |

---

### 🔍 重点词汇详解

#### 1. Mediterranean [ˌmedɪtəˈreɪniən] n.

* **含义：** (the ~) **地中海** (=Mediterranean sea，位于欧、亚、非三大洲之间)；地中海沿岸的居民。
* **adj.：** 地中海的，地中海民族的。

#### 2. complain v.

* **搭配：**
    * **complain to sb.** 向某人抱怨
    * **complain of/about sth.** 抱怨某事

#### 3. continually [kənˈtɪnjuəli] adv.

* **含义：** **连续地，频繁地** (强调**时断时续**)。
    * *例句:* The baby cry continually.
* **辨析：**
    * **continuously** [kənˈtɪnjuəsli] adv. **连续不断地** (指动作中间**没有间断**)。
    * **continue** [kənˈtɪnjuː] v. 继续，连续，延伸。

#### 4. bitterly adv.

* **含义：** **刺骨地**，**彻底地**。
* **常见搭配：**
    * **bitterly disappointed** **彻底的**失望 (*disappoint* [ˌdɪsəˈpɔɪnt] vt. 使失望)
        * *例句:* I am bitterly disappointed.
    * **bitterly cold** **刺骨地**寒冷 (*chilly* adj. 寒冷的)
        * *例句:* It's bitterly cold.

#### 5. sunshine n.

* **备注：** 也可直接用 “sun” 表示阳光。
* **短语：** **a drop of sunshine** 一缕阳光 (*a drop of* 一缕)

## 讲解精粹

### 🔍 【课文讲解】

#### 1. dream of & settle down

* *He had often dreamed of retiring in England and had planned to settle down in the country.*
    * **dream of…**：想，梦见(梦想)，幻想，向往。
        * *例句:* Frank used to dream of having a car of his own.
    * **think of…**：想 (思维的活动)，考虑。
    * **settle down**：**定居，安身，安顿**。
        * *例句:* After two years of traveling, I want to settle down now.

#### 2. no sooner...than...

* *He had **no sooner** returned **than** he bought a house and went to live there.*
    * **no sooner…than…**：**一……就……** (关联词，引导时间状语从句)。
        * **时态结构：** 主句常用**过去完成时** (had no sooner done)，than 后的从句用**一般过去时**。
        * *同义表达:* **as soon as, the moment, on doing**
    * **倒装：** 当 **no sooner** 放在句首时，主句需用**倒装**。
        * **No sooner had he arrived than he called me up.** (倒装)

#### 3. for & even though

* *Almost immediately he began to complain about the weather, **for even though** it was still summer, it rained continually and it was often bitterly cold.*
    * **almost immediately**：几乎马上，很快地 (时间上的快，常用于写作)。
    * **for** (连词)：表示**因为** (解释说明，附加的)。
        * $\ne$ **because** (一定要说的原因)。
        * **注意：** *for* 不能用于句首，且后面必须重复主语。
    * **even though** $= $ **even if**：**即使，虽然** (引导让步状语从句)。

#### 4. got a shock

* *After so many years of sunshine, Harrison **got a shock**.*
    * **got a shock**：**吓了一跳，吃了一惊**。

#### 5. as if (as though)

* *He acted **as if** he had never lived in England before.*
    * **as if + 句子**：**似乎，好像** (引导方式状语从句)。
    * **虚拟语气：** 如果从句为**过去完成时** (had done)，表示与过去事实相反，即条件是**假**的。
    * **搭配：** as if/though 通常跟在描述行为举止的动词后，如 *act, appear, feel, look, smell, sound* 等。
        * *例句:* She acted **as if she were mad**. (虚拟语气)

#### 6. more than he could bear

* *In the end, it was **more than he could bear**.*
    * **more than**：在这里表示**“超过……的范围”** (超出能力、理解、忍受范围)。
        * *例句:* This piece of news is **more than I can believe**.
    * *区别于:* **比……更多** (There were more than ten people in the room.)

#### 7. hardly...when...

* *He had **hardly** had time to settle down **when** he sold the house and left the country.*
    * **hardly…when…**：**还没来得及……就……**，用法同 **no sooner…than**。
    * **倒装：** 当 **hardly** 在句首时，主句需用**倒装**。
        * **Hardly had he opened his eyes when he was knocked out.**

---

## 🎯 【Key structures】 过去完成时

* **定义：** 表示**过去某个动作发生前完成的动作**，常与**一般过去时**连用。
* **连用词：** when, after, as soon as, (not) until, by that time, (never) before, already, for, since, just, **no sooner…than, hardly…when** 等。
* **注意：** **不能**与副词 **ago** 连用 (ago 只能与一般过去时连用)。

---

## 🔠 【Special Difficulties】 词语辨析

### 1. No sooner...than and Hardly...when

* **含义：** 意义相近 **as soon as**，但更正式。
* **结构：** 通常都与**过去完成时**连用 (had done)。
* **倒装：** 当 **no sooner** 或 **hardly** 位于句首时，句子需倒装。
    * **No sooner had he begun speaking than he was interrupted.**
    * **Hardly had he got into the bus when it began moving.**

### 2. Country and Countryside

| 单词 | 词性 | 含义 |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **country** | n. | **国家，祖国**；**乡下** (做“乡下”讲时常与 **the** 连用) |
| **countryside** | n. | **农村地区** (强调景色)，**乡下** |

### 3. Continuously and Continually

| 单词 | 含义 | 强调 | 举例 |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **continuously** | **不断地，连续地** | 动作中间**没有间断** | The river flows under this bridge continuously. |
| **continually** | **频繁地，反复地** | 动作中间**有间断但又持续很久** | It rained continually. |

---

## ✍️ 【Composition】 句型练习

| 编号 | 英文原文 | 优化后句型 | 知识点 |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | He bought an old car. It was in a very bad state. (but) | He bought an old car, **but** it was in a very bad state. | *in a bad state* (状态不太好)；*though/even though* 和 *but* **不能**连用。|
| 2 | The engine was worn out. The gearbox was full of sawdust. (The engine...not only... but...as well) | The engine was **not only** worn out **but** the gearbox was full of sawdust **as well**. | **not only... but... as well** (不仅...而且)；*worn out* (破旧不堪)；*sawdust* (锯屑)。|
| 3 | He could not drive it. He could no sell it. He could not even give it away. (neither…nor…nor) | He could **neither** drive it **nor** sell it **nor** even give it away. | **neither do sth. nor do sth. nor do sth.** (既不能也不能更不能)。|

---

## ✉️ 【Letter writing】 日期书写

* **原则：** 每年下列月份写出**全称**：3月，4月，5月，6月和7月。
* **缩写：** 剩余的月份写成缩写：Jan. (1月)；Feb. (2月)；Aug. (8月)；Sept. (9月)；Oct. (10月)；Nov. (11月)和Dec. (12月)。

---

## ❓ 【Multiple choice questions】 单项选择

| 题号 | 题目 | 正确答案 | 解析 |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 4 | He acted \_\_\_ he had never lived in England before. a. as though b. like c. as d. even if | **a. as though** | **as if = as though** (似乎，好像) 作状语，是 *act as if/though* 的习惯用法。*like* 后跟名词/代词。|
| 5 | It was more than he could bear. He couldn't bear it \_\_\_. a. more b. longer c. any longer d. no more | **c. any longer** | **not any more = not any longer** (不再)。*not more* (比...少)。*no more* 本身就表示“不再”。|
| 11 | He \_\_\_ as if he had never lived in England before. a. made b. did c. conducted d. behaved | **d. behaved** | *act* 或 **behave** (行为，表现) 后接 *as if*。*conduct* 作动词表示行为时，常作及物动词，后接 *oneself* (He conducted himself well.)。|

---

